# Stream-K candidate subset of tier1-gemm-configs for MI350 (CDNA4, gfx950).
#
# Generated by gen-streamk-configs.py. Using the smallest efficient tile,
#   grid = gemmG * ceil(gemmM / 32) * ceil(gemmN / 32)   (num_cu = 256)
# a config is kept only when it (1) over-fills the machine (grid >= num_cu, so
# StreamKDecompose can build a P >= num_cu wave decomposition rather than bailing),
# (2) has a ragged tail -- imbalance = ceil(grid/num_cu)*num_cu/grid >=
# 1.20 -- and (3) has splittable K (gemmK >= 256). Underutilized /
# GEMV shapes (grid < num_cu) are excluded: the pass can't decompose them and
# they fall to plain split-K instead. Eligible dtypes are those with fast
# atomic_add on this arch: f16, f32.
# See gen-streamk-configs.py for the full rationale.

